#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# elliptic_pi

#% text
# `elliptic_pi(n, m)` gives the complete elliptic integral of the third kind `Pi(n | m)`.

#% text
# `elliptic_pi(n, phi, m)` gives the incomplete integral `Pi(n; phi | m)`, the integral of `1/((1 - n*sin(t)^2)*sqrt(1 - m*sin(t)^2))` for `t` from 0 to `phi`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The definition is DLMF 19.2.7 with `k^2 = m`, `n` the characteristic. `Pi(0 | m)` is `K(m)`.

#% item
# Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values; `n > 1` takes the Cauchy principal value.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
elliptic_pi(0.3, 0.5)
#% output
#= 2.250376821943947

#% cell
elliptic_pi(0, 0.5) - elliptic_k(0.5)
#% output
#= 0.0

#% cell
elliptic_pi(0.3, pi/4, 0.5)
#% output
#= 0.8777133738265032

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The integral definition:

#% cell
n_integrate(1/((1 - 0.3*sin(t)^2)*sqrt(1 - 0.5*sin(t)^2)), [t, 0, pi/2]) - elliptic_pi(0.3, 0.5)
#% output
#= 0.0

